{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Common.BalancedQuantumTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Common.BalancedQuantumTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GeomSum"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.balanced_quantum_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.balanced_quantum_twist","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L85-L125","doc":"**The balanced quantum twist** (division-free form). Let `cells` (the `n`\ncells of a Young diagram `λ ⊢ n`) and `hooks` (its `n` hooks) be the\nnumerator/denominator families of the balanced quantum dimension, with equal\ncardinality `card cells = card hooks = n`. Then\n\n  `q^{Σ cellSz} · (∏ balancedNum cells) · (∏ [hookSz]_{q²})`\n    `= q^{Σ hookSz} · (∏ balancedNum hooks) · (∏ [cellSz]_{q²})`,\n\nboth sides equal to `(q²−1)ⁿ · ∏[cellSz]_{q²} · ∏[hookSz]_{q²}`. Dividing (when\nthe denominator is nonzero) gives the classical shape\n`∏bn(cells)/∏bn(hooks) = q^{ΣhookSz − ΣcellSz} · ∏[cell]_{q²}/∏[hook]_{q²}`.\nWith the Gauss sum `Σ cellSz = n(n+1)/2` and the hook identity\n`Σ hookSz = b(λ)+b(λ')+n`, the monomial exponent is exactly\n`content(λ) − n(n−1)/2` — Step 1 of `prop:binding-period-involution-statistic`.\nThe `(q²−1)ⁿ` factors match precisely because `card cells = card hooks`; no\n`q² ≠ 1` and no division are needed for this form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.prod_balancedNum_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.prod_balancedNum_factor","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L64-L83","doc":"**Product-level twist.** Over any finite family `s` with a size function\n`sz : ι → ℕ`, the product of balanced numerators factors as a global monomial\n`q^{−Σ sz}` times `(q²−1)^{|s|}` times the product of unbalanced `q²`-integers.\nThis is the general engine: apply it to the `n` cells (numerator) and the `n`\nhooks (denominator) of a quantum dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.balancedNum_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.balancedNum_factor","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L50-L62","doc":"**Balanced-numerator factorization** (the load-bearing lemma):\n`q^k − q^{−k} = q^{−k}·(q²−1)·[k]_{q²}`, as an identity of `ℤ`-powers over a\nfield with `q ≠ 0`. No `q² ≠ 1` hypothesis — it is a monomial identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.sub_one_mul_qintU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.sub_one_mul_qintU","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L45-L48","doc":"Telescoping: `(x − 1)·[k]_x = xᵏ − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.qintU_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.qintU_zero","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.qintU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BalancedQuantumTwist.qintU","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/BalancedQuantumTwist.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Unbalanced quantum integer `[k]_x = Σ_{i<k} xⁱ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}